---

## Core Prep Day (Sunday — 2.5 to 3 hours)

### Batch-Cook Proteins & Bases
- **Lentils**: 2 cups dried green/brown lentils → simmer until tender. Use for bolognese, stuffed peppers, and lunch bowls.
- **Chickpeas**: 2 cans (or 1 cup dried, soaked overnight and cooked). Roast half with smoked paprika and cumin; reserve half plain for salads and curry.
- **Tofu**: 2 blocks, pressed. Cube and bake half at 400°F/200°C with soy sauce and sesame oil for grain bowls. Crumble the other half for tofu scramble portions.
- **Grains**: Cook 4 cups dry rice or a rice-quinoa blend; also prepare 500g dry whole wheat pasta.

### Roast Vegetables
Two sheet pans:
- **Pan A**: Cubed sweet potatoes and red onions (coconut oil, salt, pepper) — for bowls and tacos
- **Pan B**: Zucchini, bell peppers, and cherry tomatoes (olive oil, oregano, garlic powder) — for pasta and salads

### Make Sauces
- **Tahini dressing**: Tahini, lemon juice, maple syrup, water, garlic
- **Peanut sauce**: Peanut butter, soy sauce, lime, ginger, sriracha, water
- **Marinara base**: Sautéed onion, garlic, canned crushed tomatoes, oregano, basil — simmer 20 min

### Prep Raw Components
- Wash and chop kale, lettuce, carrots, cucumber
- Soak 1 cup cashews (for Wednesday's cream sauce)

---

## Daily Breakdown

| Day | Breakfast | Lunch | Dinner | Snack |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Monday** | Tofu scramble (pre-crumbled tofu, turmeric, black salt, spinach) with 2 slices whole grain toast | Grain bowl: rice, roasted sweet potato, chickpeas, kale, tahini dressing | Lentil bolognese over whole wheat pasta with side salad | Apple + 2 tbsp almond butter |
| **Tuesday** | Overnight oats (prepped Sunday: oats, chia, plant milk, topped with fresh berries) |
